<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kalhana</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">12th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kalhana was a Kashmiri <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brahmins">Brahmin</a> poet and historian who wrote the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajatarangini">Rajatarangini</a>, 'River of Kings', in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sanskrit">Sanskrit</a> verse in 1148–1150. Covering the kings of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kashmir">Kashmir</a> from legendary times to his own day, it is the earliest Indian work to attempt a critical history, drawing on inscriptions, earlier chronicles and records, and it is the main source for the region's early dynasties.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Indian tradition holds other dates: Aryabhata's 3102 BCE has become widespread, the Aihole inscription of Pulakeshin II implies 3137 BCE, and Varāhamihira and <b>Kalhana</b> place the war around 2449 BCE.</blockquote><a href="/work/mahabharata">Mahabharata · Origins</a></li><li><blockquote>Almost everything known about the Gonandas comes from the Rajatarangini, the chronicle of Kashmir written by <b>Kalhana</b> in the 12th century.</blockquote><a href="/state/gonanda-dynasty">Gonanda dynasty</a></li><li><blockquote>Under Jayasimha, <b>Kalhana</b> wrote the Rajatarangini in 1148 to 1149, a Sanskrit verse history of Kashmir and one of the few true histories of early India.</blockquote><a href="/state/lohara-dynasty">Lohara dynasty</a></li><li><blockquote><b>Kalhana</b> portrays her as ruthless and cunning but effective, and she built temples and monasteries.</blockquote><a href="/state/parvagupta-dynasty">Parvagupta dynasty</a></li><li><blockquote>Avantivarman's minister Suyya cleared rocks from the Jhelum, drained marshes and built embankments, increasing rice production and lowering grain prices, as <b>Kalhana</b> records.</blockquote><a href="/state/utpala-dynasty">Utpala dynasty</a></li></ul></section>
